    feat(ctx): add /metrics Prometheus text and /api/session-summaries with loopback-only guard (T10)
    
    Add two read-only ctx observability routes and a loopback restriction on
    all four:
    
    - GET /metrics: hand-emitted Prometheus text (stdlib only, no
      prometheus/client_golang) exposing ctx_requests_total,
      ctx_tokens_saved_total, ctx_cache_hits_total,
      ctx_cache_invalidations_total, ctx_sessions_total. Same source of truth
      as /stats (observability.Snapshot over ctx_proxy_sessions), so the two
      cannot disagree. Fail-open: a missing table degrades to 200 with
      zero-valued counters (ADR-0016).
    - GET /api/session-summaries: offset pagination (limit + cursor) over
      ctx_session_summaries via Store.ListSessionSummaries, stable ORDER BY
      created_at, session_id. Response is {items, next}; fail-open to an
      empty items list.
    - requireLoopback: a non-loopback RemoteAddr (host not 127.0.0.0/8, ::1,
      or the in-process empty addr) gets 403 + a 'loopback only' body before
      the store is opened, on /stats, /stats-history, /metrics, and
      /api/session-summaries. No data leak.
    
    T09 tests now use a loopback-address doLoopback helper (httptest.NewRequest
    defaults RemoteAddr to 192.0.2.1, a TEST-NET address). Single-open
    invariant and the full internal/http suite stay green.
    
